Description: SupraLINUX KDE Plasma desktop integration metapackage
 Development metapackage for the SupraLINUX Aurora desktop baseline.
 .
 It intentionally does not depend on kubuntu-desktop. The dependency set is
 built from Plasma-visible capabilities and their required integration layers.
 .
 SupraLINUX offers the Plasma desktop session on Wayland. Plasma 6.7.4 ships
 the Wayland session descriptor and session targets from plasma-workspace;
 no separate plasma-session-wayland package is required. XWayland remains part
 of the baseline so legacy X11 applications continue to work inside the Wayland
 session. X11 libraries or compatibility components are not removed merely for
 architectural purity.
 .
 SDDM defaults are owned by supralinux-settings; Aurora configures the greeter
 to run on KWin Wayland rather than requiring a full Xorg server solely for the
 display manager.
 .
 This package is still under audit and is not a release-frozen dependency list.
